      "desc_en": "actionlint is an open-source static checker for GitHub Actions workflow files, written in Go. It validates far more than YAML syntax: it understands workflow structure, events, jobs, needs, runner labels, action inputs, and GitHub expression types. When the related dependencies are available, it can also send shell snippets to ShellCheck and Python snippets to pyflakes. This is valuable because many GitHub Actions errors otherwise appear only after a remote workflow has started. actionlint moves that feedback into local development, pre-commit, and pull-request checks.",
      "desc_ru": "actionlint — open-source статический анализатор workflow-файлов GitHub Actions, написанный на Go. Он проверяет не только валидность YAML: инструмент знает структуру workflow, события, jobs, needs, runner labels, action inputs и типы GitHub expressions. Также он умеет передавать shell-фрагменты в ShellCheck и Python-фрагменты в pyflakes при наличии соответствующих зависимостей. Инструмент особенно полезен потому, что многие ошибки GitHub Actions обнаруживаются только после запуска удалённого workflow. actionlint переносит эту обратную связь в локальную разработку, pre-commit и pull request.",
      "usage_en": "Running it without arguments from the repository root automatically checks .github/workflows/*.yml and .yaml. In CI, teams usually enable concise file-and-line output and make the job a required status check. Monorepositories can pass selected files or feed workflow content through stdin. actionlint validates workflow correctness but does not replace a full workflow security review. Controls such as pinning actions to commit SHAs, minimizing permissions, and safely handling pull_request_target need additional policy checks or specialized tools.",
