      "desc_en": "Assetfinder is an external-asset inventory tool. The tool helps build an authorized external-attack-surface inventory of domains, subdomains, DNS records, certificates, hosts, and web services. Sources may be passive, active, or mixed, so completeness and noise differ. Treat it as one control in the chain, not as a replacement for architecture analysis, manual review, and testing.",
      "desc_ru": "Assetfinder — инструмент инвентаризации внешних активов. Инструмент помогает собрать разрешённую опись внешней поверхности: домены, поддомены, DNS-записи, сертификаты, узлы и веб-службы. Источники могут быть пассивными, активными или смешанными, поэтому полнота и шум различаются. Его стоит рассматривать как одну меру защиты в цепочке, а не как замену архитектурному анализу, ручному разбору и тестам.",
      "usage_en": "In a typical team, it is normally used for attack-surface management before active testing. Define root domains, subsidiaries, exclusions, and rate limits before execution. Normalize and deduplicate passive results, then run active DNS and HTTP validation separately. Confirm every asset and assign an owner before security testing. The minimum operating loop is input and scope → pinned configuration → execution → manual validation of material signals → remediation owner → retest. If the tool acts as a gate, define the blocking rule in advance: risk level, confidence, fix availability, and permitted exceptions.",
